{"id": "q0013", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 728552883, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "Eve had 20 pieces of pomelos. After giving her friend some pomelos, Eve is left with 1/4 of the pomelos she originally had. How many pomelos did Eve give away?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0013.wav", "input_sha256": "985cf51b63efa06ff45836529161750579a6f6e7d110500e24fe9a1f665a7bed", "input_samples": 224200, "input_s": 14.012, "n_real_chunks": 15, "score": 0.1428, "act": 0.9989, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Eve had 20 pieces of pomelos to start with. After giving some away, she was left with a quarter of what she originally had. So, a quarter of 2 0 is 5. That means she gave away the rest. To find out how many she gave away, we subtract the 5 she has left from the original 2 0. Twenty minus five equals fifteen. So, E ve gave away fifteen pomelos.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 10, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 19, "feed_lag_max_ms": 621, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 809, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0013_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "d2103fd50139620df277a8baf4a7d106b194f609540e4c04166219333163b6c6", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 19.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.054, 1.097, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.055, 2.098, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.054, 3.097, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.054, 4.09